      "nets": ["Net-(U9-Pad1)", "Net-(U9-Pad2)", "Net-(U9-Pad4)"],
      "observed": "U9 (74LVC1G86 XOR gate) is present and connected: pin 1 to U1 GPIO3, pin 2 to U4 T- / J3 pin 1, pin 4 to U6 DELAY. The specification does not mention U9 or any XOR gate, and states that U4's T- pin wires directly to J3 pin 1 and that U6's DELAY pin is not used/mentioned.",
      "expected": "No U9; U4 T- should connect only to J3 pin 1; U6 DELAY should be configured per TPS1H200 datasheet (likely capacitor to GND or left unconnected), not driven by an XOR gate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U9\") (value \"74LVC1G86\") (footprint \"Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23-5\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"34\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"GPIO3/ADC1_CH3\") ... (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"35\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"T-\") ... (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"2\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"Net-(U9-Pad4)\") ... (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"DELAY\") ... (node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"4\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Thermocouple wire pair connects to a 2-pin screw terminal (J1 for U2, J2 for U3, J3 for U4) whose two pins wire directly to the MAX31855's differential thermocouple inputs T+ (pin 3) and T- (pin 2)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U9 loads the U4 thermocouple T- input, corrupting zone 3 temperature readings. It also drives the TPS1H200 DELAY pin with a logic signal derived from GPIO3 and the thermocouple, likely causing the heater switch to malfunction or have unpredictable delay, and potentially damaging the switch.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains an extra XOR gate U9 that is not in the specification and connects the U4 thermocouple T- input to the TPS1H200 DELAY pin, which would corrupt thermocouple readings and interfere with heater switch operation."
}

